From 0913d0853940075c5b46f5b6c35ae89fb0e4aa5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leonieziechmann <48921293+leonieziechmann@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 21:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] feat(data): a hydrated invoice stops on any problem
 (validation: auto)

The maintainer's decision on Q1: fail safe by default, so that nobody
sends a broken invoice by mistake, with a flag to debug it.

invoice(validation:) gets the default `auto`: "strict" when the invoice
is hydrated (data from `data:` or `--input invoice-pro-data*`), "draft"
otherwise, so an invoice without data behaves exactly as in 0.6.0. An
explicit "draft", "strict" or none keeps its meaning in both modes, and
`--input invoice-pro-validation=..` still wins: `=draft` renders the
draft (inline markers, badge, watermark, report page, no XML), `=none`
turns the checks off. Data problems stay class-`data` issues, which is
what makes the draft a debug view.

The strict stop of a hydrated invoice lists every problem and ends with
the one line that says how to debug it (contract/hydrate.typ, loaded only
when hydrated); the strict text of an invoice without data is unchanged.
resolve-level takes `hydrated:` and names `auto` among the allowed
values (the misuse pin in tests/validation/strict follows). Misuse and
the R7 panics are unchanged; zugferd-errors keeps "panic".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
